<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 67,249 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 67,249 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 67,249 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday compared to 73,062 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Wednesday   December 3</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 5,361	13,279</p>
<p>    Import cargo		61,888	59,783</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, four are expected to sail and seven are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil		67,985	 Johar		   5/12</p>
<p>Lubricating oil	 3,864	 Oriental Iris	 5/12</p>
<p>Gas oil		  35,000	 Rosebud		 Due</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     30,704	 Pan Express	   6/12</p>
<p>Tallow		    3,840	 Vanino		  8/12</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
